  "body": "The media data processing steps list ( https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#media-data-processing-steps-list ) lists \"If the media resource is found to have an audio track\" and \"If the media resource is found to have a video track\" before \"Once enough of the media data has been fetched to determine the duration of the media resource, its dimensions, and other metadata\".\r\nThe first two of these result in AudioTrack and VideoTrack objects being created. The third results in the readyState transitioning to HAVE_METADATA.\r\nDoes this ordering mean anything when the information on the duration and the tracks is available at essentially the same time? Will the track objects be created before readyState is set to HAVE_METADATA? Or will the track objects only be guaranteed to be available until readyState changes to HAVE_CURRENT_DATA?\r\nOne example of this (not the best) is when the UA supports DASH natively. In this case, both the information on the duration and the information on the tracks are included in the same file - the MPD.",
